--TEST--
A path typed on the command line reaches `Core\IO::read` through `Core\Path::fromCwd`, whose answer is a `string` without `tainted`, and the `fs` grant still bounds the file it names — `rule:security/launderers-are-sink-named`, `rule:programs/path-literals-resolve-from-their-file`
--ARGS--
notes/report.txt
../outside.txt
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every argument is `tainted`. `fromCwd` removes that qualifier, so its answer
// is a declared `string` and a path door accepts it.
foreach (Core\Cli::arguments() as tainted string $typed) {
    string $path = Core\Path::fromCwd($typed);
    try {
        echo Core\IO::read($path);
    } catch (IOError $missing) {
        echo "the os answered\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
        // The grant is `.`, and a path that climbs out of it is still refused:
        // removing `tainted` widens no grant.
        echo "refused outside the grant\n";
    }
}
--FILE notes/report.txt--
first line of the report
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
--EXPECT--
first line of the report
refused outside the grant
